---
/**
 * Lossless. FLAC depends on a lossless source being able to serve the song:
 * the user's own Qobuz account or relay, or, in official builds, the project's
 * relay (QbdlxFileUrlRouter tries them in that order). Don't promise or pitch
 * free lossless here: the project's relay gets one neutral sentence that points
 * to the privacy page, which says what it's sent.
 *
 * Downloads wait for FLAC unless Lossy fallback is on (off by default,
 * LosslessSourcePreferences; DownloadManager defers instead). Streams fall back
 * to JioSaavn (AAC) or YouTube (Opus), and Now Playing shows "via JioSaavn" /
 * "via YT".
 */
import FeatureRow from '../FeatureRow.astro';
import Icon from '../Icon.astro';
---

{/* A light phone: the Listening row above is dark. */}
<FeatureRow id="lossless" icon="graphic-eq" overline="Lossless" title="FLAC, when a source has it" screens={['queue']} theme="light" reverse>
  <p>When a lossless source has a song, Stash streams and downloads it as FLAC and shows its quality as it plays.</p>
  <p>
    The source can be your own Qobuz account or your own relay, both set up in Settings › Audio &amp; Quality.
    Official builds can also use a relay the project runs, which the
    <a href="/privacy#lossless-and-fallback-audio">privacy page</a> describes.
  </p>
  <p>
    When no lossless source has a song, it streams in AAC or Opus instead, and Now Playing shows where it came from.
    Downloads wait for FLAC unless you turn on Lossy fallback.
  </p>
  <p class="more">
    <a class="arrow-link" href="#faq-lossless">Where lossless comes from <Icon name="arrow-forward" size="18px" /></a>
  </p>
</FeatureRow>

<style>
  .more {
    margin-top: 24px;
  }
</style>
